From 45d9924780c5b872cd5bbd5e8cd5c8daaf93d07b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:21:09 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: enter L0 before calling the gadget resume callback

When the controller leaves clock gating or LPM L1, dwc2 called the
gadget driver's resume callback first and only then set lx_state to L0.
call_gadget() drops the controller lock around the callback, and a
callback that queues requests right away hit dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue()
refusing transfers outside L0 - the queue error surfaces as a stalled
control transfer and, with g_multi, as a USB link that enumerates but
never passes traffic after a suspend/resume cycle.

Set the L0 link state (and exit L1 where applicable) before informing
the gadget, matching the order the Synopsys reference flow uses.

Ported from Orchard apple-16k drivers/usb/0001 (tested on the iPad 6).
Measured here against the D21 reload link-death class: gadget still
enumerated while the ECM interface went dead 3/5 touch reloads
(2026-11-04, smc_cut_rail=0).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c | 6 +++---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c    | 8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
index 9565e6a52..0be67f27d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
@@ -390,11 +390,11 @@ void dwc2_wakeup_from_lpm_l1(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, bool remotewakeup)
 			return;
 		}
 
-		/* Inform gadget to exit from L1 */
-		call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
-		/* Change to L0 state */
+		/* Change to L0 state before informing the gadget */
 		hsotg->lx_state = DWC2_L0;
 		hsotg->bus_suspended = false;
+		/* Inform gadget to exit from L1 */
+		call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
 fail:		dwc2_gadget_init_lpm(hsotg);
 	} else {
 		/* TODO */
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
index 102169b40..07220a0bc 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -5741,8 +5741,12 @@ void dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, int rem_wakeup)
 		dwc2_writel(hsotg, dctl, DCTL);
 	}
 
-	/* Change to L0 state */
-	call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
+	/*
+	 * Change to L0 state before the resume callback: it may queue
+	 * requests right away, and dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses them
+	 * outside L0.
+	 */
 	hsotg->lx_state = DWC2_L0;
 	hsotg->bus_suspended = false;
+	call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
 }
-- 
